The hyphenation patterns under data/hyphenation/ come from two sources.

1. Patterns written for this library: cs.pat.txt, hu.pat.txt, hy.pat.txt, id.pat.txt, lv.pat.txt, mk.pat.txt and
   ro.pat.txt (Czech, Hungarian, Armenian, Indonesian, Latvian, Macedonian, Romanian). They are generated by
   bin/generate-patterns.php from syllabification rules written from scratch for this library
   (tests/Generator/SyllableRules.php), after the published orthographic rules of each language; no hyphenation
   pattern, exception list or word list under another licence was read or used to write them. They are covered by
   the MIT licence of the package, in LICENSE:

       Copyright (c) 2026 Philippe Gamache, doing business as Le Gnome Archiviste; a Parler Haut Interagir Librement
       project

2. Patterns imported from hyph-utf8 2026-02-21 (https://ctan.org/pkg/hyph-utf8), the TeX hyphenation patterns in
   UTF-8: every other <tag>.pat.txt and <tag>.hyp.txt file is a verbatim copy of hyph-<tag>.pat.txt and
   hyph-<tag>.hyp.txt, distributed under the licence stated in the header of hyph-<tag>.tex, reproduced below for
   each language. Where a file is offered under several licences, the permissive one (MIT, BSD, LPPL or a notice
   permitting copying) is the one used here. These data files are not covered by the MIT licence of the package
   code.

Not imported from hyph-utf8, because their licence does not permit them in an MIT package or because a soft hyphen
cannot express their line breaks:
- hyph-cs: GPL 2 or later only (Czech has patterns written for this library)
- hyph-hu: MPL 1.1, GPL 2 or LGPL 2.1 only (Hungarian has patterns written for this library)
- hyph-hy: LGPL only (Armenian has patterns written for this library)
- hyph-id: GPL only (Indonesian has patterns written for this library)
- hyph-lv: LGPL 2.1 or GPL 2 only (Latvian has patterns written for this library)
- hyph-mk: GPL only (Macedonian has patterns written for this library)
- hyph-ro: no licence stated (Romanian has patterns written for this library)
- hyph-sr-cyrl: GPL only (Serbian is served by sh-cyrl and sh-latn, under LPPL)
- hyph-th: Thai breaks lines without a visible hyphen, which a soft hyphen cannot express (Thai takes zero-width
  spaces between words from the ICU dictionary of ext-intl instead)


